Hi Ed

I have into a problem running a model with blavaan.

model <- '
  xi1 =~ x1 + x2 + x3 + x4 + x5
  xi2 =~ x6 + x7 + x8 + x9 + x10
  xi3 =~ x11 + x12 + x13 + x14 + x15
  xi1 ~~ 1*xi2 + xi3
xi2 ~~ xi3
'

When I run it like this,

  bfit <- bcfa(mod, dat, std.lv <http://std.lv> = F,
               adapt = adp, burnin = brn, cp="fa", ## fa srs
               sample = 5000,#inits = "prior",
               dp=dpriors(beta="dnorm(0,1/100)",
                          itheta="dt(0,1/2.5,1)T(0,)[sd]",
                          nu="dnorm(0,1/100)",
                          ipsi="dt(0,1/2.5,1)T(0,)[sd]"))

I get this type of error and it doesnt save anything in the object bfit

Error in chol.default(x, pivot = FALSE) :
  the leading minor of order 6 is not positive definite
Error in pd.solve(varcov, log.det = TRUE) :
  x appears to be not positive definite
Error in x$ind : $ operator is invalid for atomic vectors

When I run it like this,

  bfit <- bcfa(mod, dat, std.lv <http://std.lv> = F,
               adapt = adp, burnin = brn, cp="srs", ## fa srs
               sample = 5000,#inits = "prior",
               dp=dpriors(beta="dnorm(0,1/100)",
                          itheta="dt(0,1/2.5,1)T(0,)[sd]",
                          nu="dnorm(0,1/100)",
                          ipsi="dt(0,1/2.5,1)T(0,)[sd]"))

I get this type of error and it doesnt save anything in the object bfit

Error : The following error occured when compiling and adapting the model using rjags:
 Error in rjags::jags.model(model, data = dataenv, inits = inits, n.chains = length(runjags.object$end.state),  :
  Error in node (lambda[1,1,1]/psistar[2,2,1])
Invalid parent values

This happens when I fix the latent covariance to 1. I am attaching an example data set in case its useful

Thanks for all the work in blavaan

